  "prefLabel": "Saf-C 504.06 Trailer Vehicle Identification Number",
  "priorExpiration": "2012-03-15",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Saf-C 504.06 Trailer Vehicle Identification Number.\n\n(a) An application for a state issued vehicle identification number for all trailers 3,000 pounds or less shall be submitted, in person to a substation or authorized municipal agent or, in person or by mail, to:\n\nThe Division of Motor Vehicles\n\n23 Hazen Drive\n\nConcord, N.H. 03305.\n\n(b) A vehicle identification number for all trailers that are 3,000 pounds or less shall be issued only after the vehicle identification number plate on the trailer has been examined by a law enforcement officer, a licensed motor vehicle dealer, or an authorized inspection station. For trailers greater than 3,000 pounds, a NH issued vehicle identification number (VIN) shall be required.\n\n(c) Upon being issued a trailer vehicle identification number, a person shall display the sticker in a permanent and prominent place on the trailer. At no time shall a person remove or deface the sticker or any other identifying number.\n\nSource. #7972, eff 10-17-03 (See Revision Note #1 at chapter heading for Saf-C 500); amd by #8999, eff 9-29-07; amd by #9995, INTERIM, eff 9-17-11, EXPIRED: 3-15-12\n\nNew. #10135, eff 5-23-12; ss by #13521, eff 1-13-23 (formerly Saf-C 504.12) (see Revision Note #2 at chapter heading for Saf-C 500)",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/saf-c500.html"
